robably wouldn't had the  opportunity that I that I had to play in  the World Series but you know in the  early stages of rehab it was it was  different whenever the team was home I  was doing at home in the clubhouse but  whenever they went on the road I'd have  to go to a TI physical therapy meet with  some some of their people and you know  this is this make sure that we're on the  same plan and they did a great job they  made sure that I stayed on the plan you  know grinded it out with me it was great  and then going on the later parts rehab  you know my teammates really really came  up big for me you know it never stays I  wasn't you know feeling it or just down  and these guys picked me up the fans  picked me up to this I remember it's  game like 102 and I'm getting tweets and  everything like that saying herbs would  be miss via wish you're out there you  know keep keep killing rehab it was just  you know a total team effort from  everyone to you know make sure that I  was doing good and then once I got to  the doctor's visit when we were in Game  three of the NLCS saying that I got  cleared it was you know there was a lot  of emotions there because it was a fella  gave us such a long journey I know that  there's people going through a lot worse  than what I went through and but for for  everyone to have this this team effort  to make sure that that I was in good  shape and mentally and physically  it meant a lot how did you keep it under  wraps that there was even even a remote  chance of playing in postseason  I really didn't think there was I'm not  gonna lie every time I went to my  doctor's meetings down in Dallas he he  always say you know we're looking at the  second half of winter ball maybe that's  the make sure that I get some at-bats  for going into spring training and then  once I like once I said I had that  doctor's visit at game 3 and it was  probably the best  possible news that could have got at  this it just shows you the the the rehab  that